## Performance experience
Define project-specific budgets for meaningful user journeys. For web products, include relevant Core Web Vitals or equivalent field/lab metrics when the project can measure them reliably.

Performance regression checks must be stable enough to gate; noisy synthetic metrics should be treated as evidence, not blindly retried until green.

## Deterministic design verification
Select only tools appropriate to the project:
- component/unit interaction tests;
- browser/end-to-end journey tests;
- accessibility automation;
- deterministic screenshot/visual regression;
- responsive viewport matrix;
- localization/RTL fixtures;
- performance budgets.

Visual baselines are reviewed artifacts. A changed screenshot is neither automatically correct nor automatically wrong.

## Human judgment evidence
For material user-facing changes, record the smallest useful evidence: screenshots/video, keyboard walkthrough, responsive matrix, accessibility findings, or design-review notes. Do not require heavyweight ceremony for invisible/non-UI changes.

## Exceptions
Any intentional deviation from this contract must be explicit in the Work Unit/PR with rationale, impact and follow-up or owner acceptance.
